A timer line that fires stays armed.
It would signal again on every later tick;
after a tick no Irq armed on a timer line is due.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work smp-test qemu-replay
Report: armed timer line is due

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -494,7 +494,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
         }
         struct core *armed = &cores[irq->core];
         if (irq_due(irq, sched_ticks)) {
-            irq_signal(irq);
+            sched_signal(irq_notification(irq), irq->bits);
         } else if (tick_before(irq->deadline, armed->nearest_deadline)) {
             armed->nearest_deadline = irq->deadline;
         }
